    "lawCode": "Amd §50, Civ Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1235               Revised 02/03/17\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the civil service law, in relation to the promotion\nand administration of scheduled exams\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation would require the civil service department to promote\nexaminations. Additionally, civil service examinations would be\nrequired to be offered at SUNY Educational Opportunity Centers.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 - Amends section 50 of the civil service law to require that\nthe Department of Civil Service appropriately advertise and promote\ncivil service examinations.\n\nSection 2 - Amends section 50 of the civil service law to require that\ncivil service examinations be held at SUNY Educational Opportunity\nCenters.\n\nSection 3 - Effective Date - 90th Day after it becomes law.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nSUNY's Educational Opportunity Centers are located on 12 campuses of\nthe State University System and annually train over 14,000 residents\nfor entry level jobs and education related matters. By administering\ncivil service exams at these locations, the civil service will be able\nto reach historically underserved students.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016 - REFERRED TO CIVIL SERVICE AND PENSIONS\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\n90 days after enactment\n",
